# ClangSharpPInvokeGenerator response file for the libdrm and kernel-uapi DRM constants.
#
# One of three macro passes, split by the library each one speaks for; see pipewire-constants.rsp
# for why macros generate apart from the ABI pass at all. The 200-odd DRM_FORMAT_* fourcc codes are
# the bulk of what these passes emit and none of them are PipeWire's, which is what made a single
# NativeConstants class misleading about where its contents came from.
#
# --file is deliberately absent: generate.sh supplies the composite root.

# DRM_SYNCOBJ_*: the flags the libdrm syncobj timeline calls take (WAIT_FOR_SUBMIT, ...).
# DRM_CAP_SYNCOBJ_TIMELINE: what drmGetCap is asked before explicit sync is used at all.
--traverse
/usr/include/libdrm/drm.h

# DRM formats and modifiers. Kernel uapi, so the values are stable ABI. Generated to avoid
# hand-transcribing 300 fourcc codes, not because they drift.
--traverse
/usr/include/libdrm/drm_fourcc.h

--include
DRM_FORMAT_*
--include
DRM_SYNCOBJ_*
--include
DRM_CAP_SYNCOBJ_TIMELINE

# The libdrm entry points themselves (drmSyncobj*, drmGetCap) are deliberately NOT generated and
# stay hand-written as [LibraryImport] in Interop/NativeLibdrm.Imports.cs, for the same errno
# reason libc.rsp gives. Their constants come from this pass.

--include-directory
/usr/include/libdrm
--include-directory
/usr/include

--namespace
PipeWire.NET.Interop
--method-class-name
NativeLibdrm

--with-access-specifier
*=Internal

--generate
macro-bindings

--config
file=multi
codegen=preview
types=unix
